<node name="CWES Prep Notes" unique_id="1" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="1" foreground="#ec5651" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h1" weight="heavy" foreground="#ec5651">CWES Prep Notes</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Certified Web Exploitation Specialist. This file holds your methodology, module notes and exam workspace as a tree of nodes. Pick a node on the left to open it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#ec5651">The exam
</rich_text>
<rich_text>CWES is a 7-day web pentest: several real-world apps, flags as you find bugs (~10 flags, pass at 8), plus a commercial-grade report. People who have taken it say the exam labs are harder than the course and need chained attacks and a lot of enumeration.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Four parts:</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 2" foreground="#ec5651">Methodology</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your methodology, as numbered blank phases that you name and fill in your own way.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 13" foreground="#ec5651">Modules</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your notes, one per Academy module, in course order. Your methodology links back to these.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 316" foreground="#ec5651">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your exam workspace, with apps, findings, flags and a log for each day, laid out like the report.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="webs https://cnmoseman.github.io/htb-study-trackers/cwes/tracker/" foreground="#ec5651">CWES Study Tracker</rich_text>
<rich_text>: the day-by-day study plan for this cert. Check off tasks there as you go.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#d9822b">Read this first
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Enumerate every application fully before you try to exploit it, and write up each finding the moment you confirm it. Cap each vuln test at ~30 minutes, then move on.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#2f9e44">Do the reporting module
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Do the </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://academy.hackthebox.com/course/preview/documentation--reporting" foreground="#ec5651">Documentation &amp; Reporting</rich_text>
<rich_text> module from the Penetration Tester path before your exam, even though it isn't in the CWES path. It shows you how to take notes during an engagement and turn them into the kind of report HTB grades. It's built around the CPTS report, so it won't match the CWES report one for one. Take the general tips and good habits from it and apply them to the CWES report template.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#ec5651">How to use it</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>1. Work through the course in order. As you finish each module, fill in its note.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>2. Build your methodology as you go. Rename each </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#ec5651">Fill in</rich_text>
<rich_text> phase to a step in your own workflow, and add or delete phases as you need. For a new phase, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Methodology Phase</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Methodology</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>3. Fill each phase with your own checklist, commands and decision points, and link back to the module notes: select some text, pick </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Insert › Insert/Edit Link</rich_text>
<rich_text>, choose </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">To Node</rich_text>
<rich_text> and pick the note.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>4. Keep one node per tool and one per technology under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tools &amp; Technologies</rich_text>
<rich_text>. For a new one, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Tool</rich_text>
<rich_text> or </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Technology</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tools &amp; Technologies</rich_text>
<rich_text>. </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 314" foreground="#ec5651">ffuf</rich_text>
<rich_text> and </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 315" foreground="#ec5651">GraphQL</rich_text>
<rich_text> are there to start you off. Link them from your module notes and phases so the commands you use most are one click away.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>5. Each module has one child node per Academy section. Expand a module in the tree to see its sections.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>6. On exam day, start at </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 316" foreground="#ec5651">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> and work from your methodology. The main nodes are in the </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Bookmarks</rich_text>
<rich_text> menu. Click any link to jump to the node behind it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
